      "title": "Local Clusters and kubeconfig Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Local Clusters and kubeconfig Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Local Cluster Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Local tools run a ==real control plane== on your laptop for dev and testing",
                "`kubectl` just talks to whatever **API server** kubeconfig points at",
                "Every tool writes a context on create: `kind-<name>`, `minikube`, `k3d-<name>`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. kubeconfig Structure",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Default file `~/.kube/config`",
                "Override: `KUBECONFIG` env var or `--kubeconfig`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "List",
                "Holds"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "{blue:clusters}",
                  "server URL + CA"
                ],
                [
                  "{purple:users}",
                  "credentials"
                ],
                [
                  "{orange:contexts}",
                  "cluster + user + default namespace"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "current-context",
                    "sub": "used by every command",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "context",
                    "sub": "cluster + user + namespace",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "API server",
                    "sub": "kubectl talks here",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Merging Files",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "export KUBECONFIG=~/.kube/config:~/.kube/kind-dev",
                "kubectl config view --flatten"
              ],
              "note": "colon-separated list; semicolon on Windows. kubectl merges them"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "A ==context== = cluster + user + namespace. ==current-context== picks the one **every** kubectl command uses."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "kind vs minikube vs k3d",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "kind vs minikube vs k3d",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Pick a tool",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "kind",
                "minikube",
                "k3d"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Runs as",
                  "Kubernetes IN Docker, node = container",
                  "one VM or container; drivers docker, hyperkit, hyper-v, virtualbox",
                  "k3s (light Rancher distro) in Docker"
                ],
                [
                  "Extras",
                  "multi-node and HA via YAML config; built for testing Kubernetes",
                  "`addons enable ingress`, metrics-server, dashboard; `--nodes N`",
                  "fastest, lowest memory; `registry create`; `-p 8080:80@loadbalancer`"
                ],
                [
                  "Pick for",
                  "==CI==, multi-node tests",
                  "==beginners==, addons",
                  "==fast==, light, many clusters"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Create and delete",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "kind create cluster --name dev",
                "kind delete cluster --name dev",
                "minikube start -p dev",
                "minikube delete -p dev",
                "k3d cluster create dev --servers 1 --agents 2",
                "k3d cluster delete dev"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Local images",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Cluster ==cannot see== your local Docker images",
                "Load the image first, else {red:ErrImagePull}"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "kind load docker-image app:1 --name dev",
                "minikube image load app:1",
                "k3d image import app:1 -c dev"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake",
              "text": "==ErrImagePull== on a local tag means the image was never loaded."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Contexts, Users and Switching Namespaces",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Contexts, Users and Switching Namespaces",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Inspect and switch",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`current-context` is the cluster kubectl uses now",
                "`view --minify` shows ==only the active context==",
                "`use-context` switches; `--context` is a ==one-off override=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "kubectl config get-contexts",
                "kubectl config current-context",
                "kubectl config view --minify",
                "kubectl config use-context kind-dev",
                "kubectl --context kind-dev get pods"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Namespaces and users",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Scope"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`set-context --current --namespace=staging`",
                  "saved on current context"
                ],
                [
                  "`-n staging`",
                  "one command"
                ],
                [
                  "`-A`",
                  "all namespaces"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Users** hold credentials: client cert/key, token, or exec plugin (`aws eks get-token`)",
                "Two contexts can share ==one cluster== with different users or namespaces"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Wrong-context gotcha",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`use-context` ==persists across terminals==",
                "`kubectl delete` in the wrong context hits {red:prod}"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Stay safe",
              "text": "Check `current-context` first. Use `--context` explicitly in scripts. Or install kubectx/kubens: `kubectx dev`, `kubens staging`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "kubectl explain and Dry-Run",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "kubectl explain and Dry-Run",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Find fields and kinds",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`kubectl explain pod.spec.containers` reads the ==cluster's own API schema==",
                "Walk down with ==dots==; `--recursive` prints the whole field tree",
                "`kubectl api-resources`: kind, short name, API group, namespaced (`po`, `svc`, `deploy`, `ns`)"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Dry-run modes",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Flag",
                "Runs",
                "Checks"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`--dry-run=client`",
                  "Locally",
                  "Render + validate, no server contact"
                ],
                [
                  "`--dry-run=server`",
                  "API server",
                  "Full validation + admission, {green:not persisted}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. YAML skeleton workflow",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Generate",
                    "sub": "dry-run -o yaml",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Edit",
                    "sub": "web.yaml",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Diff",
                    "sub": "kubectl diff",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "x",
                    "text": "Apply",
                    "sub": "kubectl apply",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "kubectl create deployment web --image=nginx \\",
                "  --dry-run=client -o yaml > web.yaml",
                "kubectl diff -f web.yaml",
                "kubectl apply -f web.yaml"
              ],
              "note": "diff shows what apply would change"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Forgot -o yaml",
              "text": "Dry-run then prints only ==created (dry run)== and **no manifest**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Debugging with port-forward and exec",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Debugging with port-forward and exec",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. port-forward",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Tunnels `localhost:LOCAL` to container port ==REMOTE== via the API server",
                "Targets: `pod/web-1`, `svc/web`, `deploy/web`",
                "Binds ==127.0.0.1== only; pins to **one pod**",
                "Dies on pod restart; blocks the terminal",
                "`--address 0.0.0.0` only deliberately"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "kubectl port-forward pod/web-1 8080:80",
                "kubectl port-forward svc/web 8080:80"
              ],
              "note": "LOCAL:REMOTE"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. exec and debug",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Command",
                "Does"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`exec -it web-1 -- sh`",
                  "Shell; `--` splits kubectl flags from command"
                ],
                [
                  "`exec web-1 -c app -- env`",
                  "`-c` picks the container"
                ],
                [
                  "`exec web-1 -- cat /etc/resolv.conf`",
                  "One-shot command"
                ],
                [
                  "`debug -it web-1 --image=busybox --target=web`",
                  "Distroless: no shell"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Debug order",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "get pods",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "describe pod",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "logs",
                    "sub": "--previous after crash",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "exec / port-forward",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Got 'not found'?",
              "text": "You forgot ==-n namespace==. Pass it on every command."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Port-forward to svc/web?** Tunnel to one pod behind it, for debugging only",
                "**No shell in image?** `kubectl debug` with a busybox image"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cheat Sheet: Local Clusters, Contexts and Debugging",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cheat Sheet: Local Clusters, Contexts and Debugging",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Create and load",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Tool",
                "Create",
                "Load image"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "kind",
                  "`kind create cluster --name dev`",
                  "`kind load docker-image app:1 --name dev`"
                ],
                [
                  "minikube",
                  "`minikube start -p dev`",
                  "`minikube image load app:1`"
                ],
                [
                  "k3d",
                  "`k3d cluster create dev`",
                  "`k3d image import app:1 -c dev`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Unloaded image",
              "text": "Local images are invisible to the cluster: ==ErrImagePull=="
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Contexts and namespace",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "kubectl config get-contexts",
                "kubectl config use-context NAME",
                "kubectl config current-context",
                "kubectl config view --minify",
                "kubectl config set-context --current --namespace=NS",
                "kubectl get pods -n NS   # -A = all"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Explain, dry-run, debug",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "kubectl explain pod.spec --recursive",
                "kubectl create deployment web --image=nginx --dry-run=client -o yaml > f.yaml",
                "kubectl diff -f f.yaml"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Need",
                "Command"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Tunnel",
                  "`kubectl port-forward svc/web 8080:80`"
                ],
                [
                  "Shell",
                  "`kubectl exec -it POD -c CTR -- sh`"
                ],
                [
                  "Crash logs",
                  "`kubectl logs --previous POD`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Dry-run without `-o yaml` prints no manifest",
                "Forgot `-n NS`: resource not found",
                "`use-context` persists across terminals"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "You run `kubectl delete deploy web` in a fresh terminal and it hits prod, though you only used kind-dev earlier today. Why?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`use-context` is saved in kubeconfig, so it persists across terminals",
                "Fix: check `current-context` first, or pass `--context` explicitly"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`kubectl create deployment web --image=nginx --dry-run=client` prints only `deployment.apps/web created (dry run)`. Where is the YAML?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "It was never asked for: add `-o yaml`",
                "Redirect with `> web.yaml`, edit, then `apply`"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "You built `app:1` locally and a kind pod shows ErrImagePull. What is wrong and what fixes it?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Cluster nodes are containers with their own image store, so they cannot see your local Docker images",
                "Run `kind load docker-image app:1 --name dev`"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
